## Delineation

/ [RootBuildSubject] -(Delineation)> [Inside], [Outside], [References], [Uncertainty]

& [Inside] is the build governed by this specification
  + [engine] is one safe-Rust authoritative semantic core
  + [compiled_input] is admitted test-signed semantic packages and source maps
  + [semantic_fabric] is exact identities, typed relations, contextual contracts, indexes, and proof-bearing source anchors
  + [query] is parameterized subject, use-case, boundary, description, relation, and source-detail search
  + [CLI] is deterministic versioned JSON input and output around the engine
  + [Codex_adapter] is a narrow read-only MCP projection of the same core protocol after CLI proof
  + [neural_fabric] is a derived learned candidate router admitted only after deterministic baselines and adoption gates pass
  + [future_FPGA_profiles] is equivalent interpreter and native-compiled projections admitted only after the software oracle stabilizes

& [Outside] is work not authorized by the initial implementation slices
  + [provider_modification] is llama.cpp, Ollama, OpenAI, or model-internal modification
  + [hidden_state_control] is KV cache, activation, or attention-kernel mutation
  + [production_key_infrastructure] is production certificate authority, hardware key storage, and organizational signer administration
  + [distributed_deliberation] is multi-machine faculties, token rings, shared latent state, and cooperative inference junctions
  + [effect_execution] is filesystem, network, account, or public side effects authorized through retrieved SOP
  + [general_database_supremacy] is any claim that Cantor is the apex of all database systems without benchmarks
  - never: let an outside subject enter an early slice through a convenient adapter

& [References] is related signed fabric retained without absorption
  + [SOP_Core] is semantic-language behavior later consumed by the engine
  + [ReflectiveVirtualMachine] is a future execution and review consumer
  + [FacultyRuntime] is a future consumer of compiled attention programs
  + [NarrativeCantor] is a future activation supervisor

& [Uncertainty] is the explicitly gated remainder
  + [parser_coverage] is the exact SOP grammar subset required for the first compiled package
  + [cryptographic_profile] is the production signature algorithm and key-management policy
  + [physical_store] is in-memory first, then benchmark-selected persistence
  + [learned_architecture] is classifier, dual encoder, reranker, graph model, or composition
  + [training_threshold] is the measured advantage required to admit a learned router
  + [FPGA_target] is a future vendor, device, board, toolchain, interface, and resource envelope
  = must: resolve each uncertainty through its owning slice rather than global speculation

## Constraint Ledger

& [ConstraintLedger] is the source-grounded invariant set
  + [invariant] is purpose and use case are first-class query parameters
    @ [source] preserved user dictation
  + [invariant] is subject identity, included boundary, excluded boundary, and ambiguity remain distinct
    @ [source] preserved user dictation and Delineation
  + [invariant] is results may include SOP terms, clauses, source spans, definitions, conditions, relations, instructions, descriptions, and proof
    @ [source] preserved user dictation
  + [invariant] is stable semantic identity and content digest outrank live line number
    @ [source] Cantor Trusted Compilation Profile
  + [invariant] is exact identity and typed relations run before approximate association
    @ [source] Cantor Proof-Carrying Semantic Query Engine
  + [invariant] is learned weights propose while deterministic gates admit and hashes resolve
    @ [source] Cantor Neural-Routed Gated Semantic Fabric
  + [invariant] is one core protocol serves CLI, MCP, tests, and later service surfaces
    @ [source] Cantor Execution Surface Profile
  + [invariant] is the authoritative engine uses safe Rust edition 2024
    @ [source] Cantor Rust Engine Implementation Profile
  + [prohibition] is unsigned or uncompiled material cannot acquire SOP authority
    @ [source] Cantor Trusted Compilation Profile
  + [prohibition] is rankings, similarity, or path distance cannot establish truth, equivalence, or authority
    @ [source] Cantor Proof-Carrying Semantic Query Engine
  + [boundary_guard] is deterministic engine and CLI precede persistent service, embeddings, and neural training
  + [quality_constraint] is every governing result must expose why it was selected and where it came from

& [ConstraintCheckTrace] is the active-ledger grounding result
  + [passed] is every invariant and prohibition has source, user, or signed-specification provenance
  + [repaired] is neural_fabric means a derived routing projection over authoritative semantic fabric, not weights as semantic storage
  + [repaired] is line_result means a versioned display locator plus digest-bound source span, not line number as identity
  + [repaired] is all_go means begin the staged build, not waive adoption, trust, proof, or phase gates
  + [conflict] is none remaining inside the staged boundary

## Conceptual Data Design

& [SemanticUnit] is the smallest governed addressable meaning
  + [unit_uuid] is stable surrogate identity
  + [natural_key] is namespace, subject identity, context identity, semantic kind, and declared version
  + [kind] is term, clause, definition, description, use_case, boundary, condition, relation, instruction, authority, evidence, fault, or derivation
  + [normalized_meaning] is the context-bounded intended meaning
  + [status] is admitted, historical, superseded, revoked, disputed, or untrusted
  + [source_anchor_set] is one or more digest-bound source spans

& [SubjectContext] is the identity boundary for interpretation
  + [subject] is canonical or provisional focus
  + [purpose] is the intended result or decision
  + [use_case_set] is situations in which the meaning should operate
  + [include_boundary_set] is identities, contexts, roles, and criteria that belong
  + [exclude_boundary_set] is meanings, contexts, roles, and paths that must remain outside
  + [perspective_set] is applicable faculty, stakeholder, policy, or world views
  + [assumption_set] is visible provisional context

& [SemanticRelation] is a typed directed relation between semantic units
  + [relation_uuid] is stable identity
  + [source_unit_uuid] is exact source endpoint
  + [relation_type] is defines, aliases, describes, applies_to, excludes, requires, constrains, permits, prohibits, supports, contradicts, derives, supersedes, references, or continues_with
  + [target_unit_uuid] is exact target endpoint
  + [context_guard] is applicability boundary
  + [weight_account] is named deterministic and optional learned score components
  + [provenance] is compiled package and source relation

& [SourceAnchor] is authoritative source recovery
  + [package_digest] is admitted package identity
  + [document_digest] is immutable document identity
  + [span_digest] is immutable exact quoted-byte identity
  + [semantic_locator] is stable semantic declaration address
  + [display_path] is human-readable package-version path
  + [display_line_start] is current package-version line
  + [display_line_end] is current package-version line
  = must: verify span bytes before quoting

& [CompiledSemanticPackage] is immutable runtime authority
  + [package_digest] is authoritative package identity
  + [semantic_root_digest] is the unit and relation root
  + [source_root_digest] is the source and quote root
  + [manifest] is exact inputs, outputs, compiler, dependencies, and proofs
  + [recognition_certificate] is test certificate during early slices
  + [admission_state] is unexamined, admitted, quarantined, rejected, superseded, or revoked

& [SemanticFabric] is the authoritative logical model
  + [unit_store] owns SemanticUnit records
  + [relation_store] owns SemanticRelation records
  + [source_store] owns signed SourceAnchor and quote bytes
  + [exact_index] maps UUID, natural key, canonical term, alias, digest, and semantic locator to records
  + [lexical_index] is a derived non-authoritative term and clause candidate index
  + [graph_projection] is a derived traversable relation view
  + [router_projection] is an optional fabric-bound learned candidate index
  = must: designate unit_store, relation_store, and source_store as authoritative
  = must: make all other indexes recomputable and invalidatable

## Query Interface

| [RequestedDetailKind] is (term | clause | definition | description | use_case | boundary | condition | relation | instruction | authority | evidence | fault | source_span | derivation)
| [SearchMode] is (exact | contextual | relational | lexical | routed | composed)

& [CantorQueryRequest] is the complete parameterized semantic demand
  + [protocol_version] is required
  + [request_uuid] is required
  + [term_set] is input terms, aliases, clauses, semantic UUIDs, or candidate propositions
  + [subject] is canonical or provisional focus
  + [purpose] is the intended result or decision
  + [use_case_set] is expected applications and triggering situations
  + [include_boundary_set] is identities and criteria that must be preserved
  + [exclude_boundary_set] is identities and interpretations that must not be selected
  + [description_need] is brief, normal, verbose, or none
  + [requested_detail_kind_set] is one or more RequestedDetailKind values
  + [search_mode_set] is ordered allowed SearchMode values
  + [relation_type_set] is allowed typed relationship families
  + [criterion_set] is required facts, guards, versions, authorities, or states
  + [source_scope_set] is permitted package, namespace, file, or semantic-locator scope
  + [perspective_set] is applicable faculty, stakeholder, or policy context
  + [known_unit_set] is already resident unit and package digests
  + [authority_context] is caller identity and read scope
  + [budget] is maximum results, path depth, candidate count, bytes, tokens, time, and proof detail
  = must: reject a query lacking subject or purpose unless the operation is explicit low-level inspection
  = must: preserve omitted optional fields as absent rather than guessed

& [CantorQueryResult] is the bounded proof-carrying response
  + [protocol_version] is exact response schema version
  + [request_uuid] is originating request
  + [result_uuid] is immutable result identity
  + [resolved_subject_set] is selected identity and material alternatives
  + [record_set] is requested semantic details
  + [quote_set] is digest-verified exact source spans
  + [relationship_path_set] is typed applicable paths
  + [boundary_account] is included, excluded, ambiguous, contradictory, unauthorized, stale, and budget-clipped candidates
  + [association_account_set] is named score and selection components
  + [proof_bundle] is provenance, selection, applicability, relationship, derivation, and completeness proof
  + [continuation_set] is bounded next queries licensed by unresolved dependencies
  + [result_digest] is immutable output identity
  = must: return no governing record without admitted source and applicability proof

& [QueryPipeline] is the deterministic-first execution transform
  + [stage_1_validate] validates request schema and budgets
  + [stage_2_admit] limits search to admitted packages and caller scope
  + [stage_3_resolve] finds exact UUID, digest, natural key, canonical term, and alias matches
  + [stage_4_context] applies purpose, use cases, include boundaries, exclude boundaries, and perspectives
  + [stage_5_structure] filters detail kinds, relation kinds, guards, authority, and criteria
  + [stage_6_traverse] follows bounded typed relation paths
  + [stage_7_lexical] proposes text candidates when deterministic structure is insufficient
  + [stage_8_route] optionally proposes neural addresses and paths only when an admitted router exists
  + [stage_9_exact_lookup] resolves every approximate proposal through exact indexes
  + [stage_10_gate] applies trust, identity, context, purpose, relationship, authority, constraint, budget, and proof gates
  + [stage_11_rank] orders admitted candidates through inspectable component scores
  + [stage_12_project] returns the smallest sufficient records, quotes, paths, boundaries, and proof
  = must: record material admissions, rejections, reroutes, and omissions

## Inward Depth Contracts

& [CoreEngineDepthContract] is sufficient_for_implementation
  + [activation] is a validated protocol operation enters cantor_core
  + [actors] is CLI, MCP adapter, tests, and later service adapter
  + [data] is requests, packages, semantic units, relations, traces, results, and faults
  + [state_transition] is received to validated to planned to executed to proved to projected or faulted
  + [service_boundary] is pure semantic evaluation separated from I/O
  + [policy_gate] is schema, budget, trust, and authority validation
  + [proof_gate] is deterministic fixtures plus trace inspection
  + [failure] is invalid request, unavailable package, ambiguity, proof gap, budget, or internal invariant fault
  + [weave] is implements RustEngineRole and SingleEngineInvariant

& [TrustedPackageDepthContract] is sufficient_for_planning
  + [activation] is package load or query requiring an unloaded package
  + [actors] is compiler fixture, trust store, engine admission gate, and caller
  + [data] is source snapshots, semantic IR, graph, anchors, quote store, manifest, test keys, and certificate
  + [state_transition] is unexamined to admitted, quarantined, rejected, superseded, or revoked
  + [service_boundary] is compilation outside runtime query; admission inside runtime boundary
  + [policy_gate] is digest, signer scope, compiler identity, dependency lock, validity, and revocation
  + [proof_gate] is eight MinimumTrustProof cases
  + [failure] is unsigned, altered, mixed, stale, revoked, downgraded, poisoned, or scope-exceeding package
  + [weave] is constrained_by CantorTrustedCompilationProfile

& [SemanticFabricDepthContract] is sufficient_for_implementation
  + [activation] is an admitted package is loaded or a query plan requests an index
  + [actors] is compiler fixture, SemanticStore, QueryPlanner, and optional router
  + [data] is units, relations, contexts, anchors, indexes, projections, and invalidation records
  + [state_transition] is empty to loaded to indexed to queried to invalidated or superseded
  + [service_boundary] is logical semantic model independent from physical persistence
  + [policy_gate] is exact identity, version, context, and package membership
  + [proof_gate] is index equivalence and recomputation produce the same canonical results
  + [failure] is identity collision, orphan relation, stale projection, cycle, or index/source mismatch
  + [weave] is implements LogicalSemanticTables and FourPlaneArchitecture address and relation planes

& [QueryEngineDepthContract] is sufficient_for_implementation
  + [activation] is a validated CantorQueryRequest
  + [actors] is caller, QueryPlanner, QueryExecutor, ProofBuilder, and ResultProjector
  + [data] is request, plan, candidates, gates, score account, result, proof, omission, and trace
  + [state_transition] is query received to normalized to planned to executed to validated to projected
  + [service_boundary] is read-only semantic operation with separately owned caches and traces
  + [policy_gate] is exact-before-approximate, bounded traversal, visible ambiguity, and proof completeness
  + [proof_gate] is contextual alias fixture, negative unsigned fixture, and query/result replay
  + [failure] is unknown, ambiguous, no authority, stale, contradictory, cycle, proof gap, or budget exhaustion
  + [weave] is implements SemanticQueryPlan and SOPQueryRequest

& [CLIDepthContract] is sufficient_for_implementation
  + [activation] is cantor receives a subcommand and structured request
  + [actors] is human, Codex subprocess, script, and test harness
  + [data] is protocol envelope on standard input, result on standard output, diagnostics on standard error, and exit class
  + [state_transition] is process start to parse to execute to emit to exit
  + [service_boundary] is adapter only; no interface-specific semantic rules
  + [policy_gate] is bounded input, no shell-secret arguments, read-only initial operations, and explicit failure
  + [proof_gate] is golden JSON envelopes and semantic equivalence with direct cantor_core calls
  + [failure] is invalid JSON, protocol mismatch, trust failure, unresolved dependency, policy denial, or internal fault
  + [weave] is implements CantorCLI and CodexCLIIntegration

& [CodexToolDepthContract] is sufficient_for_planning
  + [activation] is Codex selects a Cantor semantic-read tool
  + [actors] is Codex, MCP adapter, cantor_core, and user
  + [data] is MCP request schema projected to CantorQueryRequest and result projected without semantic loss
  + [state_transition] is discovered to invoked to validated to returned or faulted
  + [service_boundary] is one read-only MCP tool over the same protocol
  + [policy_gate] is readOnly annotation, local scope, caller budgets, and no fabricated fallback
  + [proof_gate] is equivalent CLI and MCP requests yield equivalent semantic and proof envelopes
  + [failure] is unavailable tool, schema drift, timeout, partial result, or adapter/core version mismatch
  + [weave] is later phase of ExecutionSurfaceProgression and proven llama.cpp tool seam

& [NeuralRouterDepthContract] is blocked_by_adoption_gates
  + [activation] is deterministic query baseline reports a measured candidate-search cost or recall gap and a compatible router artifact exists
  + [actors] is corpus builder, trainer, evaluator, router adapter, deterministic gates, and reviewer
  + [data] is fabric digest, address vocabulary, relation vocabulary, training examples, hard negatives, model artifact, calibration, and routing proof
  + [state_transition] is proposed to trained to evaluated to admitted, degraded, invalidated, superseded, or rejected
  + [service_boundary] is candidate proposal only; exact records and authority remain deterministic
  + [policy_gate] is fabric compatibility, held-out evaluation, safe abstention, no authority bypass, and deterministic fallback
  + [proof_gate] is top-k address recall, relation accuracy, calibration, unsafe-route rate, proof recovery, and cost comparison
  + [failure] is leakage, memorized authority, stale coverage, opaque gate, hash hallucination, context collapse, or no baseline advantage
  + [weave] is implements AdoptionGate only after deterministic engine evidence exists

## Subcomponent and Cross-Weaving Trace

& [SubcomponentWeaveTraceSet] is the source-origin and local-fabric review
  + [query_parameters] derives from user-requested subjects, use cases, boundaries, descriptions, and result details and weaves into SemanticQuery
  + [source_lines] is refined to digest-bound SourceAnchor display locators and weaves into QuoteIntegrity
  + [semantic_fabric] is refined into authoritative stores plus derived indexes and weaves into DataDrivenDesign source/projection separation
  + [neural_fabric] is refined into fabric-bound candidate router and weaves into deterministic AdoptionGate
  + [CLI] derives from user build request and weaves into CantorProtocolEnvelope
  + [Codex_tool] derives from the proven external tool seam and weaves into MCP only after CLI equivalence
  + [proof] derives from the intended inspectability and weaves into ProofBundle
  + [revision_result] is accepted_after_role_refinement

& [CrossWeaveTrace] is the relation to existing Cantor fabric
  + [edge] is CoreEngineDepthContract implements CantorRustEngineImplementationProfile
  + [edge] is TrustedPackageDepthContract constrained_by CantorTrustedCompilationProfile
  + [edge] is SemanticFabricDepthContract implements CantorProofCarryingSemanticQueryEngine
  + [edge] is QueryEngineDepthContract implements CantorSOPQueryMicrokernel
  + [edge] is CLIDepthContract implements CantorExecutionSurfaceProfile
  + [edge] is CodexToolDepthContract depends_on CLIDepthContract and tool reflection proof
  + [edge] is NeuralRouterDepthContract depends_on deterministic SemanticFabricDepthContract and QueryEngineDepthContract proof
  + [conflict_edge] is immediate neural training conflicts_with existing neural AdoptionGate
  + [weave_gap] is production cryptographic profile remains outside early test-signing slices

## Requirement Set

& [RequirementSet] is the atomic implementation collection
  + [CEB-001] is create one Cargo workspace with cantor_core and cantor_cli
  + [CEB-002] is define versioned semantic unit, relation, context, anchor, package, query, result, proof, trace, and fault machine forms
  + [CEB-003] is pass the eight SOP CoreAcceptance fixtures with inspectable traces
  + [CEB-004] is compile or load one immutable test-signed package with exact source spans and semantic addresses
  + [CEB-005] is reject unsigned, modified, stale, revoked, mixed, or scope-exceeding fixture packages
  + [CEB-006] is implement exact indexes independently from labels and live line numbers
  + [CEB-007] is accept subject, purpose, use cases, included boundaries, excluded boundaries, descriptions, requested details, relations, criteria, authority, and budgets
  + [CEB-008] is query exact identity and context before typed traversal, lexical association, or learned routing
  + [CEB-009] is return requested SOP records, verified quotes, relationship paths, boundary accounts, omissions, and proof
  + [CEB-010] is distinguish ambiguity, unknown, invalid, unauthorized, stale, contradictory, and budget-clipped results
  + [CEB-011] is expose read-only query and inspect operations through a deterministic CLI JSON protocol
  + [CEB-012] is keep stdout machine-only, stderr diagnostic-only, and exit classes stable
  + [CEB-013] is prove direct-core and CLI semantic equivalence
  + [CEB-014] is expose one read-only Codex MCP tool only after CLI protocol stability
  + [CEB-015] is prove CLI and MCP semantic equivalence and visible tool failure
  + [CEB-016] is establish deterministic correctness, latency, recall, proof, and cost baselines before neural routing
  + [CEB-017] is build a provenance-preserved routing corpus only from reviewed outcomes
  + [CEB-018] is bind every learned router to exact fabric, address, relation, corpus, and model digests
  + [CEB-019] is permit learned routing to propose candidates but never authorize, resolve, or prove them alone
  + [CEB-020] is invalidate stale router coverage and preserve deterministic fallback
  + [CEB-021] is preserve one versioned Cantor protocol across Rust, interpreter FPGA, and native FPGA
  + [CEB-022] is define FPGAExecutionEnvelope and fail closed on every binding mismatch
  + [CEB-023] is define a bounded Cantor bytecode and software interpreter model
  + [CEB-024] is implement one FPGA interpreter target only after bytecode and software equivalence stabilize
  + [CEB-025] is define a statically synthesizable Cantor hardware subset and lowering contract
  + [CEB-026] is compile one measured deterministic query kernel through hardware IR or HLS to RTL
  + [CEB-027] is prove normalized result, proof, omission, and fault equivalence at every evidence level
  + [CEB-028] is record latency, throughput, area, memory, power estimate, compile time, and reconfiguration cost
  + [CEB-029] is preserve signed-package authority, mandatory gates, exact source resolution, and software fallback
  + [CEB-030] is prevent FPGA acceleration and neural routing from jointly bypassing deterministic authority

## Acceptance and Fault Gates

& [AcceptanceSet] is the completion proof surface
  + [A1] is cargo build, test, format, lint, and release build pass
  + [A2] is every CoreAcceptance fixture emits inspectable before, decision, after, proof, and fault state
  + [A3] is one test package produces stable semantic identities after source lines shift and recompilation
  + [A4] is query fixtures recover the intended contextual identity and preserve excluded meanings
  + [A5] is term, clause, description, use-case, boundary, condition, relation, instruction, source-span, and proof requests return typed results
  + [A6] is every quote verifies against its package span digest
  + [A7] is CLI golden tests and direct-core equivalence pass
  + [A8] is Codex MCP equivalence passes before the adapter is called ready
  + [A9] is no neural router is admitted without signed baseline, metric, failure, and fallback evidence
  + [A10] is any admitted router preserves zero mandatory-gate bypass
  + [A11] is any FPGA profile proves semantic and fault equivalence to the Rust reference oracle
  + [A12] is any admitted FPGA image is bound to protocol, compiler, toolchain, target, package, plan, and bitstream digests

& [FaultSet] is the visible failure surface
  + [fault] is raw_file_authority
  + [fault] is line_number_identity
  + [fault] is context_collapse
  + [fault] is boundary_erasure
  + [fault] is opaque_rank
  + [fault] is rank_as_truth
  + [fault] is unsigned_package
  + [fault] is stale_projection
  + [fault] is poisoned_index
  + [fault] is protocol_drift
  + [fault] is prose_success_parsing
  + [fault] is silent_fallback
  + [fault] is neural_authority_bypass
  + [fault] is training_leakage
  + [fault] is stale_router_coverage
  + [fault] is premature_physical_database_commitment

## Seven-Fold Explosion Trace

& [FoldTrace] is the bounded exhaustion record
  + [fold_1_edge_probe] is user request to minimum executable subject
  + [fold_1_gain_delta] is engine, fabric, query parameters, result details, CLI, and learned routing became distinct build subjects
  + [fold_1_pruned] is one monolithic neural database engine
  + [fold_2_edge_probe] is query input to authoritative source output
  + [fold_2_gain_delta] is CantorQueryRequest, CantorQueryResult, SourceAnchor, boundary account, and ProofBundle formed
  + [fold_2_pruned] is line number or model score as authority
  + [fold_3_edge_probe] is conceptual meaning to physical implementation
  + [fold_3_gain_delta] is authoritative stores separated from exact, lexical, graph, and router projections
  + [fold_3_pruned] is database-first and neural-first physical commitment
  + [fold_4_edge_probe] is named components to inward implementation depth
  + [fold_4_gain_delta] is six depth contracts with activation, actors, data, transitions, service, policy, proof, lifecycle, and failure
  + [fold_4_pruned] is feature labels without executable boundaries
  + [fold_5_edge_probe] is local depth to existing Cantor fabric
  + [fold_5_gain_delta] is subcomponent and cross-weave traces against signed query, trust, Rust, CLI, and neural profiles
  + [fold_5_pruned] is duplicate semantic authorities and an isolated MCP implementation
  + [fold_6_edge_probe] is intended mature architecture to safe build order
  + [fold_6_gain_delta] is deterministic core, trust fixture, query, CLI, MCP, persistence, corpus, and router adoption gates
  + [fold_6_pruned] is immediate daemon, distributed agents, production keys, or learned routing
  + [fold_7_edge_probe] is implementation readiness to measurable completion and reroute
  + [fold_7_gain_delta] is atomic requirements, acceptance gates, visible faults, feature-support slices, and reprocessing triggers
  + [fold_7_pruned] is further abstract expansion without new build obligation
  + [exhaustion_state] is phase_locked_with_implementation_slices

& [PruningTrace] is preserved cut material
  + [quarantined] is neural weights as semantic storage because it violates authority and explainability
  + [deferred] is physical database selection until query shape and baseline evidence exist
  + [deferred] is production cryptographic administration until test-package trust proofs pass
  + [deferred] is resident daemon until reload, concurrency, or notification cost justifies it
  + [outside] is provider modification and hidden-state intervention
  + [uncertainty] is learned model family and acceptance threshold pending deterministic measurements

& [GrowthSeedSet] is the next healthy frontier
  + [seed_1] is Cargo workspace and semantic IR acceptance fixtures
  + [seed_2] is test-signed package compiler and admission fixture
  + [seed_3] is deterministic proof-carrying query engine
  + [seed_4] is CLI and Codex adapter equivalence
  + [seed_5] is persistence benchmark from observed query shapes
  + [seed_6] is reviewed routing corpus and deterministic baseline
  + [seed_7] is bounded router experiment only after prior gates
  + [seed_8] is FPGA interpreter software model and explicit hardware target after the deterministic protocol stabilizes

& [ExplosionQualityGate] is passed for staged specification authoring
  + [coverage_check] is passed
